Here's how to collect an **assembly loading fusion trace** on .NET 8 / Linux:

### 1. Enable the runtime's assembly-load tracing

```bash
# Environment variables – set before launching your app
export COREHOST_TRACE=1          # host-level tracing (probing paths)
export COREHOST_TRACEFILE=host_trace.log

# EventPipe trace for managed AssemblyLoader events
dotnet-trace collect \
  --providers Microsoft-Windows-DotNETRuntime:0x4:4 \
  -- dotnet ./YourApp.dll
```

Provider `0x4` is the **Loader** keyword; verbosity `4` = Informational.

### 2. Catch the inner exceptions

`ReflectionTypeLoadException.LoaderExceptions` contains the **per-type** failures. Log them explicitly:

```csharp
try
{
    var types = assembly.GetTypes();
}
catch (ReflectionTypeLoadException ex)
{
    foreach (var inner in ex.LoaderExceptions)
        Console.Error.WriteLine(inner);
}
```

### 3. Hook AssemblyLoadContext events

```csharp
var alc = new PluginLoadContext(pluginPath);

// Fires when the default probing fails
alc.Resolving += (ctx, name) =>
{
    Console.WriteLine($"[Resolving] {name} in {ctx.Name}");
    return null; // let it fail visibly
};

AssemblyLoadContext.Default.Resolving += (ctx, name) =>
{
    Console.WriteLine($"[Default.Resolving] {name}");
    return null;
};
```

### 4. Quick checklist

| Symptom | Likely cause |
|---|---|
| `FileNotFoundException` in LoaderExceptions | Dependency not alongside the plugin or not in `deps.json` |
| Version mismatch / `FileLoadException` | Plugin compiled against a different version of a shared assembly |
| Only some types fail | Those types reference a missing transitive dependency |

### 5. Analyze the trace

```bash
# Convert EventPipe trace to human-readable format
dotnet-trace convert host_trace.nettrace --format Speedscope
# Or grep the host trace directly
grep -i "assembly" host_trace.log | head -60
```

The combination of **`COREHOST_TRACE`** (probing paths) + **`dotnet-trace` Loader events** (managed resolution) + **`LoaderExceptions`** logging will pinpoint exactly which assembly or dependency is missing or mismatched.
